 "comment": "What to bring in cold water (the blue badge beside the rowing light) and how the lake maps draw the shore, which the app (ios/RowFrog/Limits.swift ColdWaterKit, LakeView.swift ColdShore) and the website (web/public/app/logic.js coldWaterKit, lake.js coldShore) must both give. Below the life-jacket limit (15 °C, or the user's own `ownLifeJacket`) or below 10 °C: a life jacket; below 10 °C also a partner boat for a boat that may be a single (the starting boat `small`, any 1x), else near the shore. The shore is `cool` with the life jacket alone and `cold` below 10 °C. `kit` and `shore` null: nothing. Expected values come from a separate implementation of the rule. Read by ios/RowFrogTests/ColdWaterTableTests.swift and web/tests/coldwater.test.mjs; change it together with both.",
